   <cac:ProcurementProject>
      <cbc:Name languageID="ENG"> Works Supervision for Lot 1. Construction of Overpass (Transport Interchange) over Т-18-01 Rivne - Zdolbuniv - Mizoch - Dubno Road at km 49+590, Rivne region and for Lot 2. Construction of Multi-level Transport Interchange at the Junction of Roads M-06 Kyiv-Chop km 372+400 and M-19 Domanove (towards Brest) - Kovel - Chernivtsi - Terebleche (towards Bucharest), Rivne region.</cbc:Name>
      <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">The overall objective of the assignment is to select a qualified Consultant (the “Engineer”) to provide comprehensive contract administration and construction supervision services under of a Works Contract based on the FIDIC Conditions of Contract.  The objective of this assignment is to ensure that the Works are implemented in a timely, cost-effective, and technically compliant manner. The Engineer will be responsible for supporting the successful execution of the Project in accordance with the applicable Ukrainian legislation, the provisions of the European Investment Bank (EIB) Finance Contract, the relevant Grant Agreement, and all applicable technical standards, norms, and procedures.</cbc:Description>
      <cbc:ProcurementTypeCode listName="contract-nature">services</cbc:ProcurementTypeCode>
      <cbc:Note languageID="ENG">The procurement procedure will be conducted under a restricted procedure, followed by Quality and Cost-Based Selection (QCBS) with an 80/20 weighting (technical/financial).
Only Consultants who are shortlisted during the first stage (prequalification) will be invited to submit full proposals. The evaluation will be based on the technical quality of the proposal and financial offer.
Eligibility and Qualification Criteria:
Applicants must demonstrate:
1.	Experience in at least 3 (three) contracts involving the construction supervision of roads/ motorways/  highways, including associated civil works (e.g. overpasses, bridges with steel and/or reinforced concrete structures).
The above referneces should be implemented under FIDIC Conditions of Contract or equivalent contractual arrangements. For a contract to be considered equivalent to FIDIC, it must include:
o	Clearly defined roles for the Employer (Client), Engineer, Contractor, and DAB;
o	A Supervision Engineer acting on behalf of the Employer;
o	Fair risk allocation between parties;
o	A Dispute Arbitration Board or equivalent dispute resolution procedure in line with FIDIC principles.
2.	Experience in projects related to construction supervision of roads/ motorways/ highways, where a scope and complexity is in line with the current assignment, as specified in Requirements in Section VI. 
Contract references with the cost of Works below 10 mln EUR will not be considered
3.	Experience as a sole consultant or a lead partner in a JVCA in the execution at least two (2) supervision contract of civil works on roads/ motorways/ roads with a value equivalent each of at least 3 300 000 (three million three hundred thousand million) EUR.
4.	Minimum average annual total revenues of EUR 3.500.000,00 (three million five hundred thousand EUR) equivalent, within the last five (5) financial  years (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023 and 2024)
For all type of references the contracts must be either completed or substantially completed (i.e. at least 80% of the total contract value invoiced corresponding to the relevant scope).
The assignment requires that the Consultant demonstrate capacity in managing multi-disciplinary teams, reporting under EIB requirements, environmental and social compliance, and performance monitoring throughout the project lifecycle.
The construction Works are scheduled to commence in the first quarter of 2026 (Q1 2026), subject to the successful completion of the procurement procedure and subsequent award of the Works Contract. The Time for Completion is planned for Lot 1 Works: 28 (twenty-eight) months; and for Lot 2 Works: 32 (thirty-two) months, followed by a 12 (twelve) month Defects Notification Period (DNP). An additional 1 (one) month is allocated for pre-commencement and mobilisation activities. Completion of the Project is expected in the third quarter of 2029 (Q3 2029).
</cbc:Note>
